WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.420
What are his powers?

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:02.540
What's up with the bad guy?

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:04.500
Do superheroes have a group chat or what?

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.810
Riding on the high of the mischievous, hilarious,
and sometimes touching film, we want to clear

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:12.440
up a couple questions about Billy Batson and
his bigger, better self.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.680
Shazam! opens with the creation of the villain,
Thaddeus Sivana.

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:20.740
Bullied and belittled by his family, he is
naturally tempted by the voices of the Seven

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.109
Deadly Sins, who promise power and respect.

00:00:23.109 --> 00:00:25.900
He fails the wizard's test and is forever
scarred.

00:00:26.029 --> 00:00:30.520
The wizard casts a spell to seek the pure
of heart and find someone worthy of his name.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.220
When Billy Batson takes the test, things go
differently.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.160
"Billy Batson.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:39.420
I choose you."

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.100
The Sins aren't there to tempt him, and the
wizard chooses him as Champion.

00:00:44.109 --> 00:00:48.460
Sivana's research indicates that hundreds
of people had been found before Billy, and

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:49.720
each had in some way failed.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:51.460
Were they all sinners at their core?

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.780
Why was the wizard so picky in the first place?

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:58.120
The wizard had been burned before, bequeathing
his power to Teth-Adam, who became a tyrant

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.989
and unleashed the Seven Deadly Sins.

00:00:59.989 --> 00:01:04.129
Originally, Black Adam, as portrayed by Dwayne
"The Rock" Johnson himself, was set to appear

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:04.800
in the film.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:08.460
Perhaps we'll see exactly what happens when
a wizard gives power to someone not so pure

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.720
of heart in the Black Adam solo film.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:15.600
There are rarely hard and fast rules for magic,
which makes its implementation confusing.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:20.760
In Shazam!, Sivana, Billy, and countless other
people are spirited away to a cave-like lair

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.280
known as the Rock of Eternity.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.480
There, the wizard resides surrounded by empty
thrones.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.760
The Seven Deadly Sins are imprisoned in stone.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:32.700
This place isn't on any map, much to the frustration
of Sivana, who dedicates his life to finding

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:33.200
it.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.880
It's in a kind of limbo that can only be accessed
through magic.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:40.500
According to the comics, the Rock of Eternity
resides within multiple dimensions at once.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.780
This helps explain a thoroughly confusing
sequence during which Billy and his new family

00:01:44.789 --> 00:01:48.960
run around the maze-like rock and discover
a collection of doors straight out of Monsters

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:49.460
Inc.

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:52.000
Behind each one, there's some kind of strange
other world.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:55.500
The movie's explanation of all this is basically
just, "Because magic."

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.600
People typically don't fund mad scientists.

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:02.970
They are forced to work in abandoned castles
and basement labs, their only friend a typically

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.660
inept and malformed crony, but not Dr. Sivana.

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:09.060
He has a couple dozen scientists working under
him in a busy lab.

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:13.080
Only when you walk into his personal office
does his lifetime obsession with the mystical

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:16.320
Rock of Eternity and Seven Deadly Sins begin
to show.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:20.150
Sivana has been especially smart to hide his
desperate search into the realm of unknowable

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:22.660
magic as a study of "mass hallucination."

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:27.580
Sivana Industries seems to be a lucrative
business, on par with Wayne Enterprises and

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:28.080
Lexcorp.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:32.540
It is also a "family company," as emphasized
from the patronizing video that plays in the

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:33.700
building's elevator.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:38.520
Maybe Sivana Industries is involved with mental
health or behavioral studies in the DC Extended

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:42.520
Universe, which would have allowed Sivana
to inconspicuously study magic under his alibi.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:47.020
Plus, if there have really been so many wizard
abductions, that seems like a worthy phenomena

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:48.020
to look into.

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:52.200
The Seven Deadly Sins are evil, powerful,
and seriously ugly.

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:53.739
The rest of the details are fuzzy.

00:02:53.739 --> 00:02:54.790
Are they demons?

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:56.320
The actual Seven Deadly Sins?

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.799
According to the film, they are manifestations
of the worst of mankind.

00:02:59.799 --> 00:03:04.090
In the comics they were known as the Seven
Deadly Enemies of Man, which de-emphasizes

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:06.040
the Judeo-Christian connection.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:10.600
The comics also explain exactly how they carry
out their chaotic plans, which seems to involve

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:12.460
causing as much misery as possible.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:17.740
Envy, Greed, Wrath, Gluttony, Lust, Sloth,
and Pride speak sweet nothings to their victims,

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:20.360
promising that they'll give them whatever
their hearts’ desire.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:22.480
They do give power, but at a cost.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:26.920
The Sins possess their victims, so Sivana's
own evil tendencies were amplified.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:30.500
"Demon" might not be the most correct terminology,
but they sure look the part.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:34.160
In the world of Shazam, just about anything
seems possible.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.920
Superheroes can be spotted flying.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.280
There are secret kingdoms beneath the waves.

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:41.300
Superman sometimes shows up in high school
cafeterias.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:45.680
And according to the lore artfully detailed
in Wonder Woman, the Greek pantheon was very

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:47.360
real and very powerful.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:52.210
They were all killed by Ares, except for Zeus,
who created the Amazonians to protect humanity

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:53.640
from the god of war's wrath.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:58.450
Shazam's powers are derived from and equivalent
to some of the most famous names in mythology,

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:01.640
which suggests that perhaps they themselves
had been involved with the wizards on the

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:02.700
Rock of Eternity.

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:05.880
When Billy grasps the staff of the wizard
- which yes, um..

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:06.560
Phrasing?

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:11.040
Is that still a thing?... he is gifted with
the wisdom of Solomon, the strength of Hercules,

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:15.830
the stamina of Atlas, the power of Zeus, the
courage of Achilles, and the speed of Mercury,

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:17.480
who goes by his Roman name.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:19.960
The first letters of their names spell out
SHAZAM.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:21.960
"Shazam."

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:23.800
"Are you for real?"

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:24.440
"Say it!"

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:24.940
"Okay!

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:26.280
Shazam?"

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:30.660
Billy doesn't seem to be too wise when it
comes to handling his powers responsibly,

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.760
but his lightning hands are certainly Zeus-like.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:37.830
The first scenes of the film have the Sins
lined up conveniently in the Rock of Eternity.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:41.380
They're just as terrible in stone as they
are in the flesh, when Sivana absorbs them

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.160
and takes them into the mortal plane.

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:46.980
When he confronts the board of his father's
company, the sleek conference room quickly

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:49.660
crowds when seven demonic entities crash the
meeting.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:53.940
Even though they exist in smoke and dust in
Sivana's evil eye, they are solid when they

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:56.400
unceremoniously rip into the board members.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:01.640
Lust has tentacles, Greed an extra set of
arms, Gluttony a huge mouth with big teeth,

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:07.210
Envy a goblin-like appearance, Sloth has sloth
arms, and Pride has huge bat wings and horns.

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:11.070
The comics mention that Pride might be the
most dangerous of all the Seven Deadly Sins,

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:14.440
but the winged nightmare seems content to
give center stage to its buddies.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.780
It isn't a surprise when Freddie's YouTube
videos of "Captain Sparklefingers" or the

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:20.260
"Red Cyclone" go viral.

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:25.020
In the DCEU, YouTube must be filled with quick
moments of superheroes caught on tape.

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:28.680
What's surprising is that people in the movie
aren't all that enthralled with a new hero

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:30.990
whose powers seem to rival those of Superman's.

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:34.520
Remember that this is in the same universe
where Superman was compared to a god.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:38.640
Shazam only manages to gather a small crowd
of admirers when he's showing off his lightning

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:39.140
hands.

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:44.080
The tone of Shazam! marks a notable departure
from the very serious, dark, and gritty films

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:45.420
of the DCEU.

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:49.580
Instead of digging into the international
uproar from the appearance of another superhuman,

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:51.800
the movie focuses on the kids in the cast.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:56.040
Director David F. Sandberg has said that he
mined the Spielberg-directed adventures of

00:05:56.050 --> 00:06:00.070
his childhood and the expertise of the kids
on set for a more fun tone.

00:06:00.070 --> 00:06:04.740
Shazam! is a family film, so there are Fortnite
references instead of bloody death scenes.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:10.780
Shazam is one of very few superhero characters
that is genuinely stoked to be a superhero.”

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:12.740
Is Shazam overpowered?

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:17.490
The twist that saved everyone's bacon when
things looked darkest was that Billy, as Champion,

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:19.420
could share his power with his family.

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:24.370
With the shout of "Shazam!" and a burst of
lightning, all the kids get a superhero makeover:

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:27.040
all adult, athletic, and ultra-powerful.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:30.860
They each seem to have a particularly strong
dose of one of Shazam's signature powers,

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:34.610
whether that's speed for Darla, flight for
Freddie, or strength for Pedro.

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:38.360
Though it seems all of Shazam's powers have
been split among the kids, Billy still has

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:39.220
his full arsenal.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:43.200
This suggests that Billy could have made a
whole army of superheroes before he snapped

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.820
the wizard's magical staff in half.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:48.760
This may have been part of the wizard's grand
scheme, considering the empty thrones on the

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:49.760
Rock of Eternity.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:54.200
It would be up to the new Champion to fill
them, and Billy expedites the process by creating

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.460
five new Shazams.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.280
The kids in the Vasquez house are pretty smart.

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:03.040
Eugene, for example, is a next-level computer
whiz who manages to track down Billy's birth

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:03.540
mother.

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:05.760
They think fast and are incredibly perceptive.

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:10.340
They adjust relatively well to being introduced
to a world of supervillains and smoke monsters.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:14.570
They seem to instantly recognize the ugly
monsters in Sivana's eye as Sins.

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:17.750
Mary realizes that they are somehow connected
to how strong Sivana is.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:20.430
Did we miss the part where they were given
an explanation?

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:22.680
They've proven time and again to be quick
studies.

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:24.240
Freddie is a superhero expert.

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:27.440
"You're the only person I know who knows anything
about this caped crusader stuff."

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:30.720
Mary did everything she could to get into
her dream college.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:34.740
Even quiet Pedro was the one to find Billy's
book full of leads on the location of his

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:35.240
mom.

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:39.000
As it turns out, Envy is actually one of the
more dangerous Sins.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:43.300
It stays cozied up in Sivana's evil eye for
as long as possible, until Billy manages to

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:45.000
finally provoke it out of hiding.

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:45.900
Why Envy?

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:49.000
The Sins work by preying on base instincts
and feelings.

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:53.420
Envy's the most powerful feeling for Sivana,
because he envies Billy for having been chosen

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:54.600
as Shazam's Champion.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:58.940
Envious and bitter, he makes himself into
the Sins' Champion to spite the wizard who

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:00.240
said he wasn't good enough.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:03.360
Envy eats him up inside and without it, he
was powerless.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:07.780
The end credit scenes after superhero movies
are often clues for what's to come.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:12.040
Usually only the most ardent of comics fans
know exactly what's happening in these brief

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:13.460
snatches of exposition.

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:17.920
In the mid-credits scene from Shazam!, when
Sivana is seen madly scribbling graffiti on

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:22.080
his prison cell, we start to understand the
importance of that little caterpillar seen

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:23.260
at the Rock of Eternity.

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:27.700
His name is Mister Mind, and he's one of the
most diabolical creatures in the DC Universe.

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:32.580
As his name suggests, he's super smart, and
he uses his incredible intellect for evil.

00:08:32.599 --> 00:08:36.840
In the comics, this little worm had the plan
to assemble the Monster Society of Evil.

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:40.880
Sivana is likely the first recruit, having
teamed up with Mister Mind in the comics many

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:41.900
times before.

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:45.930
Mister Mind also has mind control powers,
which probably come in handy when trying to

00:08:45.930 --> 00:08:46.930
take over the world.

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:51.220
We've yet to see exactly what his plans are
in the DCEU, but they are not good.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:55.440
It's easy to assume that most superheroes
know each other, or are at least aware of

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:56.540
each other.

00:08:56.540 --> 00:09:00.680
Powerful figures like Superman or personalities
like Aquaman's are hard to miss.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:03.180
Justice League allowed them to really get
to know each other.

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:06.850
For Billy, these are still legendary figures
akin to celebrities.

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:10.540
He's probably just as excited as Freddie to
meet Superman for the first time.

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:12.790
In the comics, Supes and Billy go way back.

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:17.200
Black Adam, the aforementioned Champion-gone-bad,
is powerful enough to make even the almighty

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:18.200
Superman balk.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:23.220
It takes the combined might of Shazam and
Superman to take him down in the 2010 animated

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:26.360
movie Superman/Shazam!: The Return of Black
Adam.

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:31.080
With a Black Adam film on the way, presumably
with a slightly grittier feel than Shazam!,

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:34.120
the Superman cameo might be connected with
Black Adam's return.

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:39.180
Maybe Superman needed information from Shazam
about a similarly powered villain on the rise.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:42.220
Or maybe he's something of a welcoming committee
for new superheroes.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:46.620
At least he would have felt the need to check
out a new, ultra-powerful hero just to make

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:49.040
sure he doesn't have any villainous tendencies.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:51.620
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:55.120
Plus, even more Looper videos about Shazam!
are coming soon.

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:59.200
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

